title scooter_read -- the held read view, a scroll position paged over a channel
prompt recur: continue the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send often; Rye-first; approve own design rounds; stop at custody gates
think Prior lap landed render_window (the scroll position wired to the drawn frame). Its recommend named the next rung: bind navigation over a HELD position. Two ways to reach a keyboard: extend dexter_key to decode Up/Down/Page as first-class kinds (it maps them to .ignored today, a proven contract), or first build the held position the keys will drive.
think Chose the held position first -- smaller, self-contained, does not reopen dexter_key's decode contract in the same lap (one keystone per round). scooter_read is scooter_compose's READ-side twin: where compose holds the write prompt, read holds the scroll top.
think Design: View owns one u32 top; verbs (opened/go_home/go_oldest/page_up/page_down/line_up/line_down) delegate to scooter_scroll clamped against the channel's live post_count; render delegates to scooter_view.render_window at the held top. page_rows = view.body_rows - 1, matching render_window's reserved status row, so a page up reveals exactly the posts the status marked older above. Values apart, never braided: scroll keeps the math, view keeps the drawing, this keeps the position.
think The channel is passed to each verb rather than stored, so the view never outlives or aliases a channel it does not own -- the same custody care scooter_compose takes with its channel pointer.
obs Six cruxes GREEN on metal over a 30-post journal (page_rows 22): a fresh view opens at home (top 8) and its render anchors seq 29 to the last body row, byte-for-byte render_window at its top; paging up steps back one page to the first post and clamps at 0; paging down returns to home (8) and clamps; a line up/down moves by exactly one at each edge; a 4-post journal stays home with every paging verb a no-op and renders the elder face exactly; and the strongest -- walking oldest-to-home by line steps, the view's render equals render_window at its top at EVERY stop, so the held position and the drawn slice are one truth.
obs GREEN first metal run, no reds. Elder witnesses unaffected (new module, imports scooter_channel/scooter_scroll/scooter_view same-dir, no cycle). tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, >=2 positive // invariant asserts per fn (before-and-after position bounds), no seam cast.
loom witness=scooter_read_witness cruxes=6 journal_posts=30 page_rows=22 walk=oldest_to_home_by_line result=GREEN
file pond/apps/scooter_read.rye the held read view: one bounded scroll position, paging verbs clamped against the live journal, render is render_window at the held top
file tools/scooter_read_witness.rish builds the module and asserts the six cruxes GREEN on metal
file session-logs/20260817-110428_scooter-read-held-view.kyri this record
recommend keep-going the read view now has a held position and a faithful render; the next rung binds a keeper's keys to it -- extend dexter_key to decode Up/Down (arrows) and Page Up/Down as first-class key kinds (they map to .ignored today, a proven contract to update with its witness), then a small binding maps those keys to scooter_read's page/line verbs; the raw TTY read and the Comlink wire between two Constel piers reach the serve gate, the maintainer's hand
